              },
              "size": 38,
              "link": null
            },
            {
              "id": "108:1027",
              "name": "[What brought you here? Describe the event, your role, and the idea or question you explored in a short personal note.]",
              "w": 620,
              "h": 100,
              "text": "Over two weeks at Kode with Klossy, I learned SQL and Tableau while exploring how data can tell stories about topics that matter. My team created “Women in STEM: Education Paths and Career Outcomes,” a dashboard examining global STEM education and U.S. workforce participation.",
              "font": {
                "family": "Inter",
                "style": "Regular",
                "variationSettings": {
                  "wght": 400,
                  "slnt": 0
                }
              },
              "size": 17,
              "link": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "108:1029",
          "name": "Highlights",
          "w": 380,
          "h": 404,
          "layout": "VERTICAL",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "108:1030",
              "name": "The moments I’m keeping",
              "w": 380,
              "h": 55,
              "text": "The moments I’m keeping",
              "font": {
                "family": "Instrument Serif",
                "style": "Regular"
              },
              "size": 38,
              "link": null
            },
            {
              "id": "108:1031",
              "name": "[One thing you made or contributed] [One thing you learned] [A person, conversation, or moment that stayed with you]",
              "w": 380,
              "h": 325,
              "text": "Sourced datasets on Kaggle and refined our focus after early data challenges.\n\nWireframed the dashboard and built interactive Tableau visualizations of degree attainment, fields of study, and employment outcomes.\n\nUsed peer feedback to improve our work and presented it on Pitch Day.\n\nExplored equity in AI, ethical innovation, and inclusive technology in Culture of Tech sessions.",
              "font": {
                "family": "Inter",
                "style": "Regular",
                "variationSettings": {
                  "wght": 400,
                  "slnt": 0
                }
              },
              "size": 17,
